Tradically, HIV is spreading rapidly in some parts of China as a result of transvalidation of infected blood.
However, the number of people infected with HIV in this way is reduced to almost zero, the health services of China said at a conference in Yunnan province.
However every year the number of those who live with HIV and spin in China increases by 100,000.
Transmitting HIV through sexual intercourse is a serious problem in the LGBT community in China.
Homosexuality was decriminalised in 1997, but discrimination against people in KGBT communities has been widely rampant.
According to surveys due to conservative values, 70-90% of men who have had sexual intercourse with men end up marrying women.
A lot of cases of disease transmission are a result of misguided protection in these relationships.
In 2003, the government of China pledged to provide universal access to medicines for HIV as part of an effort to deal with the problem.
