A South Korean legislator has claimed the number of fugitives from North Korea to South Korea has declined since Kim Jong-un came to power seven years ago.
Bieong Sug, quoting data from South Korea's unification ministry, said there were 1,127 fugitives last year, with 2,706 by comparison in 2011.
